===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|knobelouch}}, with dissimilation from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|chlobalouh|lit=[[clove]]-[[leek]]}}; compare {{m|de|klieben||cleave}} and {{m|de|Lauch||leek}}. The initial ''kl-'' was later adapted to the large group of terms for thick objects beginning with ''kn-'' (cf. {{m|de|Knopf}}, {{m|de|Knoten}}, {{m|de|Knolle}}, etc.). The same in {{cog|nl|knoflook}}.

